index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3cf6bd60dece8a30b760ed683f2d05b17b1cd30d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# V2 bounded Avalanche wire review
+
+Based on native worktree `42793b5f2`. The pinned ABC `src/net_processing.cpp`
+version handler reads sender nonce and trailing extra entropy (absent values are
+1); avahello signs delegation id, sender nonce, receiver nonce, sender entropy,
+receiver entropy in that order. Session retains those actual exchanged fields.
+The immutable active transcript is exposed through Transport and Dispatcher.
+No shared nonce or caller-supplied authentication transcript is accepted by the
+adapter. Root supplies the local version entropy and secret-key signing callback.
+
+Only an explicit profile supporting capability 16 enables Avalanche application
+messages. Profiles with mandatory features 7 and transaction relay 8 retain their
+existing behavior. A profile requiring Avalanche sets required_features |= 16.
+Without 16, incoming Avalanche commands remain bounded ignored optional commands;
+Transport/Dispatcher refuse outgoing Avalanche commands.
+
+ABC's proof, delegation, hello digest, poll, signed response digest/signature,
+Block inventory type 2, Proof inventory type 0x1f000001, compact proof shortids and
+differential request indices retain pinned formats/cryptography. V2 avaproof
+extends ABC proof serialization with a CompactSize vector of native Payment lock
+byte vectors, ordered one per signed stake. Each lock must be 35 bytes with
+PUSH32 and the native Payment suffix. V2 avaproofs uses the same compact keys,
+6-byte shortids and differential prefill indices; each prefill is that same V2
+ProofEnvelope rather than an unbound ABC proof. This negotiated extension is
+necessary because native lock commitments are absent from upstream proofs.
+Every variable count (stakes, payout script, pubkeys, delegation levels, polls,
+responses, prefills, lock vectors, inventory and requests) is scanned before ABC
+container deserialization. Full payload/frame caps remain independent.
+
+Discovery currently emits zero prefills and requests every non-prefilled slot.
+This conservative collision fallback does not infer proof identity from a shortid
+and does not measure a discovery bandwidth optimization. Native prefills are
+accepted and admitted. Root callbacks perform native proof/UTXO validation,
+quorum binding, real fenced chain observation and poll-engine vote application.
+The adapter never creates voting policy or chain decisions. sent_proof_inventory
+is called only after Dispatcher accepts an avaproofs action.
+
+Drain Application notices independently of diagnostic output. Demultiplex mixed
+type-1/type-Proof Application inventories before delivering proof-only messages
+to this adapter. Deliver activation, call Activate, send Hello, and deliver all
+Avalanche Application notices to Handle. Retain the notice when it returns
+Backpressure. Call Tick to expire bounded requests and Pump to retry the front
+outbound action. Busy/capacity/terminal dispatcher results retain the action;
+explicit Disconnect releases it and invokes runtime quorum/query disconnection.
+Poll Backpressure requires retaining the original OutgoingPoll; do not allocate
+a replacement query. Root supplies one stable local session public key and owns
+its matching private key. Callbacks must not reenter the single-owner adapter.
+
+The standalone test uses actual Session/Transport/Dispatcher framing through
+fragmented bounded memory byte streams and an isolated temporary runtime home.
+No daemon, live network, production data, wallet, Chronik or published assets are
+used. The corpus fixture was copied from peer_dispatcher_test at the base; only
+explicit initial monetary anchors were added for current runtime compatibility.
+
+```sh
+cmake -S src/lotus_v2/avalanche_peer_test -B /tmp/v2-ava-peer -G Ninja \
+  -DLOTUS_ABC_BUILD=/path/to/pinned/abc/build \
+  -DLOTUS_SECP_LIBRARY=/path/to/pinned/abc/build/src/secp256k1/libsecp256k1.a \
+  -DLOTUS_BOOST_INCLUDE=/path/to/boost/include
+cmake --build /tmp/v2-ava-peer --target avalanche_peer_test
+/tmp/v2-ava-peer/avalanche_peer_test
+```
+
+Checks include actual negotiated nonce/entropy orientation, authenticated hello,
+unauthenticated poll rejection, typed block poll and real Schnorr response,
+invalid signature isolation, compact discovery/native envelope relay, native
+prefill admission, proof truncation/trailing/oversized count rejection, mandatory
+native binding and action retention under dispatcher Busy.
